# Copy to .prod.env — credentials for the PRODUCTION Cloudflare account.
# Read by deploy.sh --prod only; dev keeps using `wrangler login`.
#
# Prod lives in a separate Cloudflare account (wisdom.ops) so it can be handed
# over on its own. wrangler stores exactly ONE login session, so the account is
# selected with these two variables instead — they outrank the login, leaving
# the personal one untouched. The GitHub Action will set the same two names as
# repo secrets, so CI later is this path, not a different one.
#
# Token: ops account -> My Profile -> API Tokens -> "Edit Cloudflare Workers"
# template, scoped to that account. Account ID: Workers & Pages -> overview.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# Name of the production Pages project, created FROM THE OPS ACCOUNT.
# Deliberately blank: the name is still open (static-web-hosting.md, open-Q #2),
# `<project>.pages.dev` is a single global first-come namespace, and a Pages
# project cannot be moved between accounts — one created from the wrong login
# would have to be deleted, briefly freeing the name to anyone. deploy.sh fails
# loudly rather than guessing.
CF_PAGES_PROJECT_PROD=
